Z||000005||85 gt fiero||12-30-2001||04:49 PM||||whats so wrong with that company i havnt heard of them so could someone tell me why there so bad  thanx<P>------------------<BR>17 YEAR OLD WITH A RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES, LIGHT BARS, SCS SUSPENSION, KONI ADJUSTERS,HIGH POINT CUTOFFS,||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||12-30-2001||07:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85 gt fiero:<BR><B>whats so wrong with that company i havnt heard of them so could someone tell me why there so bad  thanx<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Outlaw had some VERY BAD quality items. They took way too much work to make nice. Lots of cracks, gaps, pits, and seam lines made them hard to fit if at all. They were also very bad at shipping items if at all. There are some folks here who ordered items, paid for them but never received them. Or they sent the items back due to the poor quality and never received their money back. They have been reported to Ebay and the FBI for internet fraud.<P>I think in the other thread the person says they are not Outlaw but that they bought the molds/rights from them. It just seems funny that the same pics are used, the same ISP for the Email is the same, and the same style ad's are used. If it is true he bought the molds and stuff from Outlaw, they probably ripped him off too and he's just trying to make back his money. The poor quality of the molds is going to make that hard to do. When buying fiberglass parts, your best bet is to spend the slightly higher costs to get the higher quality items. There are many folks here who make the same/simular parts or know where to get quality parts.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Elvira||12-31-2001||08:21 AM||||Damn, I had a feeling it might be. <BR>Hey Ferrari_Momo, I know you have something in the works as far as chin spoilers go. How long before they are available?<P>Same thing here.  I really want a chin spoiler.  I was thinking of taking the 85GT fascia off our 86GT that we are trying to sell, but I think it might sell better WITH the fascia on it (even though noone wants it!).  So I am back to square one.  Ferrari_momo, could you please keep us posted as to any progress and availability of chin spoilers?  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles<BR>84 Indy<BR>87 4-seater||||reg||1
